values
  ('p-cocoandeve-tripeptide-hair-density-serum', 'Coco & Eve Tripeptide Hair Density Serum', 'Coco & Eve', 'hair', 'physical', 'A lightweight, leave-in scalp serum in a 2.03 fl oz (60 ml) bottle from Coco & Eve''s Boost Therapy line. Coco & Eve says it uses two branded ingredient blends, Redensyl and Procapil, plus caffeine, panthenol and a probiotic ferment to reduce thinning and shedding and make hair look denser. Apply a few drops to a clean, dry scalp once a day, ideally at bedtime, and don''t rinse. It is sold as a cosmetic for both women and men.', '$35 for 2.03 fl oz (60 ml) on cocoandeve.com and on Amazon', 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51xmpBxUvcL._AC_SL500_.jpg', 'https://www.cocoandeve.com/products/tripeptide-hair-density-serum', '["coco & eve","coco and eve","boost therapy","hair","scalp","hair serum","thinning","shedding","peptide","caffeine","redensyl","procapil","cosmetic"]'::jsonb, '["skin-hair"]'::jsonb, '["cocoandeve.com","Amazon"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Sold as a cosmetic; not an FDA-approved drug for hair loss. The FDA-approved over-the-counter treatment for women is minoxidil (see below).","materials":"2.03 fl oz (60 ml) dropper bottle, leave-in. Coco & Eve says it has no added fragrance and is vegan, sulfate-free, silicone-free and paraben-free; ayna did not independently verify those claims. It contains coconut oil and a small amount of sodium metabisulfite (a sulfite preservative).","recalls":"No recalls found.","sideEffects":"Coco & Eve''s product page lists no warnings. Patch test first if you have a sensitive scalp, and stop if you get redness or itching.","opinionAlerts":"The headline numbers (+214% hair growth in 10 days, +10,200 new hairs in 3 months, +29% denser hair) are labeled by Coco & Eve as \"Redensyl testing,\" meaning tests of the ingredient, not of this serum. Coco & Eve also calls the serum \"clinically proven\" but doesn''t say how many people were tested, for how long, or whether there was a comparison group."}'::jsonb, 'Coco & Eve says the serum is clinically proven to visibly increase hair density in four weeks and to stimulate hair growth activity in 10 days, and that it reduces hair loss and gives thicker hair bulbs after 4 months. The specific percentages on the page come from testing of Redensyl, one of its ingredient blends, not of this serum. Coco & Eve doesn''t publish how many people tested the serum itself or whether there was a comparison group, and no published study of this product was found.

The best human evidence for Redensyl is a 2020 Greek trial of 44 adults with pattern hair loss (41 finished, 23 of them women). They used a lotion combining Redensyl with a second active (Sepicontrol A5) or a vehicle lotion twice a day for 24 weeks. In the active group, the ratio of growing to resting hairs rose from 2.25 to 6.02 and most people rated themselves moderately improved. It was single-blinded, tested a combination product rather than Redensyl alone, and the abstract doesn''t report how the active group compared with the vehicle group.

Caffeine has one notable trial: in 210 men with pattern hair loss, a 0.2% caffeine scalp liquid did about as well as 5% minoxidil after 6 months. That trial was in men and wasn''t blinded, and Coco & Eve doesn''t publish its caffeine concentration. No published study of Procapil on its own, in women, was found that ayna could read.

If you have thinning hair, a dermatologist can check for causes and discuss treatments with stronger evidence. Minoxidil is the over-the-counter hair-loss treatment the FDA has approved for women.', 'On cocoandeve.com it shows 4.8 out of 5 stars from 317 reviews. On Amazon it has 4.4 out of 5 stars from 297 ratings; 71% are five stars and 7% are one star. Amazon reviews range from "my hair is NOTICEABLY thicker" after a couple of weeks to "Doesn''t work" and "makes it soo greasy."', 'No published study of this serum was found. Its headline numbers come from tests of Redensyl, whose best human study tested a combination lotion in 44 adults. Caffeine did about as well as minoxidil in one trial in men.', 'brand', 'Product claims are sourced from Coco & Eve; no independent clinician endorsement verified by ayna.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"whereToBuyLinks":{"cocoandeve.com":"https://www.cocoandeve.com/products/tripeptide-hair-density-serum","Amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DF2G14KF"},"ingredients":"Full ingredient list per Coco & Eve: Aqua (Water), Butylene Glycol, Glycerin, Propanediol, Panthenol, 1,2-Hexanediol, Caffeine, Trisodium Ethylenediamine Disuccinate, PPG-26-Buteth-26, PEG-40 Hydrogenated Castor Oil, Caprylhydroxamic Acid, Sorbitol, Lactic Acid, Cocos Nucifera Oil, Xanthan Gum, Ceratonia Siliqua Gum, Larix Europaea Wood Extract, Glycine, Sodium Metabisulfite, Zinc Chloride, Camellia Sinensis Leaf Extract, Apigenin, Oleanolic Acid, Lactobacillus Ferment Lysate, Biotinoyl Tripeptide-1, Sodium Benzoate, Potassium Sorbate. Coco & Eve''s FAQ also mentions red clover extract, which is not in this list.","doctorOpinionShort":"The big percentages are from tests of one ingredient (Redensyl), not this serum. Redensyl''s best human study was a 44-person trial of a combination lotion, and caffeine''s best trial was in men. No published study of this serum was found. Minoxidil is the FDA-approved OTC option for women.","doctorOpinionCitations":[{"url":"https://www.cocoandeve.com/products/tripeptide-hair-density-serum","label":"cocoandeve.com: Tripeptide Hair Density Serum, ingredients and claims"},{"url":"https://www.cocoandeve.com/blogs/news/clinically-tested-hair-serum","label":"cocoandeve.com: 10 Days, 214% Fuller Hair (brand blog post)"},{"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32473084/","label":"PubMed: A randomized, single-blinded, vehicle-controlled study of a topical active blend (Redensyl + Sepicontrol A5) in androgenetic alopecia (Dermatol Ther 2020)","chipLabel":"Redensyl combination lotion, 44 adults (2020)"},{"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29055953/","label":"PubMed: Caffeine-based topical liquid 0.2% vs minoxidil 5% in male androgenetic alopecia, open-label randomized trial (Skin Pharmacol Physiol 2017)","chipLabel":"Caffeine vs minoxidil trial, 210 men (2017)"},{"url":"https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cder/daf/index.cfm?event=overview.process&ApplNo=021812","label":"FDA (Drugs@FDA): NDA 021812, Women''s Rogaine 5% minoxidil foam, over-the-counter","chipLabel":"FDA: minoxidil for women"}],"whoItsFor":["People with thinning hair or extra shedding who want a non-drug, leave-in cosmetic scalp serum","People who prefer a formula with no added fragrance","Not a substitute for seeing a dermatologist about new, sudden or patchy hair loss"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per Coco & Eve: use once a day, ideally at bedtime.","steps":["Apply a few drops to a clean, dry scalp, focusing on the areas that need extra care.","Gently massage it into the scalp.","Don''t rinse it off."],"sourceUrl":"https://www.cocoandeve.com/products/tripeptide-hair-density-serum","sourceLabel":"cocoandeve.com: Tripeptide Hair Density Serum"},"warnings":["Contains coconut oil and sodium metabisulfite (a sulfite): patch test first if you react to either.","Already using minoxidil or another medicated hair-loss treatment: check with a healthcare professional before combining.","Sudden, patchy or postpartum hair loss: see a dermatologist rather than self-treating."],"ingredientScience":[{"name":"Redensyl","text":"Coco & Eve says Redensyl targets hair follicle stem cells and that Redensyl testing showed +214% hair growth in 10 days and +29% denser hair; those are ingredient tests, not tests of this serum. In a 2020 single-blinded trial, 44 adults with pattern hair loss (41 finished: 18 men, 23 women) used a lotion with Redensyl plus a second active, Sepicontrol A5, or a vehicle lotion twice daily for 24 weeks. In the active group (n = 26), the ratio of growing to resting hairs rose from 2.25 to 6.02, 7.7% had great improvement and 73.1% moderate improvement, with no significant side effects. The product combined two actives, and the abstract doesn''t compare the active group with the vehicle group.","citations":[{"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32473084/","label":"PubMed: A randomized, single-blinded, vehicle-controlled study of a topical active blend in the treatment of androgenetic alopecia (Katoulis et al., Dermatol Ther 2020)"}]},{"name":"Caffeine","text":"In a 2017 open-label, randomized trial of 210 men with pattern hair loss, a 0.2% caffeine scalp liquid was not inferior to 5% minoxidil after 6 months: the share of hairs in the growth phase improved 10.59% with caffeine and 11.68% with minoxidil. The trial was in men only and wasn''t blinded. Coco & Eve doesn''t publish its caffeine concentration.","citations":[{"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29055953/","label":"PubMed: An open-label randomized multicenter study assessing the noninferiority of a caffeine-based topical liquid 0.2% versus minoxidil 5% solution in male androgenetic alopecia (Dhurat et al., 2017)"}]},{"name":"Procapil (biotinoyl tripeptide-1, apigenin, oleanolic acid)","text":"Coco & Eve says Procapil combats follicle aging and prevents hair loss, and that it gives thicker hair bulbs after 4 months. All three Procapil components appear in the ingredient list. ayna did not find a published study of Procapil on its own, in women, that it could read, so this claim is the brand''s.","citations":[{"url":"https://www.cocoandeve.com/products/tripeptide-hair-density-serum","label":"cocoandeve.com: Tripeptide Hair Density Serum, Procapil claim"}]}],"scientificCitations":[{"url":"https://www.aad.org/public/diseases/hair-loss/types/female-pattern","text":"American Academy of Dermatology: Female pattern hair loss","summary":"The AAD says the FDA has approved 2% and 5% minoxidil as a non-prescription treatment for female pattern hair loss and calls it the most-recommended treatment. This is general guidance, not product-specific validation."}],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"amazon","url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DF2G14KF","text":"Amazon: Coco & Eve Tripeptide Hair Density Serum reviews","summary":"4.4 out of 5 stars from 297 ratings on Amazon as of October 2026."},{"platform":"website","url":"https://www.cocoandeve.com/products/tripeptide-hair-density-serum","text":"cocoandeve.com: Tripeptide Hair Density Serum customer reviews","summary":"4.8 out of 5 stars from 317 reviews on Coco & Eve''s own site."}]}},"integrations":[],"badges":[],"isEmergingBrand":false}'::jsonb)
